data: {"messages":[{"content":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"18ed18cd-409d-4ef7-a5db-3b2f8147e62a"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_event_impact</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to evaluate the impact of an external event such as rainstorm, sports event, traffic control, holiday, emergency, or policy intervention on regional trajectory volume.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_event_impact/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_od_flow</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks for OD flow analysis, origin-destination matrices, commute corridors, migration routes, or region-to-region movement aggregation from staypoints.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_od_flow/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_region_heat</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to compute regional activity heat, check-in volume, point density, unique users, or Top-K active geohash regions from trajectory records.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_region_heat/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to compute trajectory-based isochrones, reachable areas, travel-time accessibility, radiation range, or real mobility coverage from a starting geohash.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>anonymize_trajectory_data</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to anonymize, desensitize, privacy-protect, differentially perturb, k-anonymize, hash user IDs, grid-generalize, or prepare sensitive GPS/check-in trajectory data before retrieval or LLM analysis.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/anonymize_trajectory_data/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>classify_trajectory_state</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to classify each user's trajectory into motion states such as stationary, directed migration, frequent circulation, random walk, cruising, long-stay, or semantic mobility behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/classify_trajectory_state/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>clean_trajectory</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to clean raw GPS, check-in, signaling, taxi, or user mobility trajectory files by validating coordinates and timestamps, removing duplicates, filtering abnormal speed jumps, and exporting standardized cleaned trajectory points.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/clean_trajectory/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_flow_anomaly</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to detect macro-level mobility flow anomalies, including abnormal region heat, check-in spikes, OD flow spikes, sudden decreases, or unusual time-window activity.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_flow_anomaly/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_route_anomaly</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to detect individual trip or route anomalies, such as unusually long distance, unusually long/short duration, abnormal average speed, detours, or trips that deviate from a user's usual behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_route_anomaly/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_trajectory_cooccurrence</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to detect co-occurrence, companion trajectories, contact tracing, crowd gathering, group convergence, or multiple users appearing in the same space-time window.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_trajectory_cooccurrence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>extract_stay_points</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to extract stay points, dwell events, OD endpoints, or meaningful stops from GPS, check-in, signaling, taxi, or cleaned trajectory data.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/extract_stay_points/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>forecast_region_flow</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to predict future people or vehicle flow for target regions, based on historical regional activity series or raw trajectory points.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/forecast_region_flow/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>fuse_spatial_evidence</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to combine hotspot, anomaly, profile, forecast, and event-impact outputs into a unified ranked regional evidence view.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/fuse_spatial_evidence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>map_spatial_grid</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to map latitude/longitude trajectory records, staypoints, trips, or check-ins into spatial grids such as Geohash for aggregation and downstream spatial analysis.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/map_spatial_grid/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>measure_spatiotemporal_entropy</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to measure spatiotemporal entropy, mobility diversity, regional vitality, flow complexity, inflow-outflow variety, or urban activity index.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/measure_spatiotemporal_entropy/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>mine_trajectory_patterns</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to discover frequent travel patterns, recurring commuting sequences, repeated geohash chains, or multi-stop trip patterns from staypoints.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/mine_trajectory_patterns/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>predict_next_location</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to predict next location, next stop, future geohash, likely destination, destination inference, or Markov-chain mobility prediction from historical trajectories.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/predict_next_location/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>profile_urban_region</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to identify urban functional regions such as residential, commercial, transit, leisure, or mixed-use areas by combining trajectory activity and POI evidence.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/profile_urban_region/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>search_similar_trajectory</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to find historical trips or trajectory records similar to a target trip based on start/end position, travel distance, and duration.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/search_similar_trajectory/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>search_spatiotemporal</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to search or recall trajectory records by time window, hour range, geohash prefix, bounding box, city, or semantic text condition.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/search_spatiotemporal/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"3788c1f8-3735-4ef7-8a93-6766710aa782"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。\n识别场景：时空轨迹 (spatiotemporal_trajectory)；场景模式：multi；候选场景：spatiotemporal_trajectory, video_surveillance\n任务切分：\n- 请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。\n任务规划：\n1. 读取输入视频文件，解析帧率、分辨率与时间戳基准，按固定采样间隔提取关键帧并建立帧序列索引，产出可供视觉模型逐帧处理的结构化帧数据集\n2. 调用视频监控场景的目标检测能力，在每一帧中定位潜在目标区域并按预设类别阈值进行筛选，输出仅包含“人员”与“车辆”两类对象的边界框坐标及置信度指标\n3. 依托时空轨迹分析能力，将连续帧中的同类别检测框进行跨帧关联与身份ID维护，依据坐标偏移量计算运动方向与步长特征，生成带唯一标识的时序位置记录序列\n4. 对关联后的轨迹数据进行完整性校验与噪声过滤，剔除坐标突变或断链片段，按照对象类别、精确时间戳及路径点阵格式进行标准化重组，形成可回溯的结构化轨迹表\n5. 汇总全量目标的类别标签、时间序列与完整运动轨迹数据，按统一Schema导出为数据文件或API响应格式，确保字段映射清晰并满足下游系统调用要求\n场景任务：\n- spatiotemporal_trajectory: 持续记录人员及车辆的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据\n- video_surveillance: 识别视频里的人员和车辆\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"3e14e93e-31ce-4511-94e9-c119a9ab6bcd"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":361,"prompt_tokens":12494,"total_tokens":12855,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":202,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":361},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":12494}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-cf2b82d6-9b3f-99b8-8ea7-e3f4f26aae22","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f8f6c-2c35-7841-975d-30cf4d3853a8-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"ask_clarification","args":{"question":"请提供需要分析的视频文件路径或名称。您是希望我：(1) 在本地数据目录中查找视频文件，还是 (2) 您有特定的视频文件需要上传？另外，是否需要重点关注特定类型的目标（如仅行人、仅车辆，或全部类型）？","clarification_type":"missing_info","context":"需要视频文件才能执行目标检测和轨迹跟踪分析","options":"[\"在 /mnt/datasets 中查找视频文件\", \"我将上传视频文件\", \"其他路径\"]"},"id":"call_a1ca61d59bf84464b905d397","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":12494,"output_tokens":361,"total_tokens":12855,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":202}}}],"thread_data":{"workspace_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/30f29ae5-9eae-480a-b1ac-6a9ecb1fae58/user-data/workspace","uploads_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/30f29ae5-9eae-480a-b1ac-6a9ecb1fae58/user-data/uploads","outputs_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/30f29ae5-9eae-480a-b1ac-6a9ecb1fae58/user-data/outputs"},"artifacts":[],"raw_messages":[{"content":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"18ed18cd-409d-4ef7-a5db-3b2f8147e62a"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_event_impact</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to evaluate the impact of an external event such as rainstorm, sports event, traffic control, holiday, emergency, or policy intervention on regional trajectory volume.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_event_impact/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_od_flow</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks for OD flow analysis, origin-destination matrices, commute corridors, migration routes, or region-to-region movement aggregation from staypoints.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_od_flow/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_region_heat</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to compute regional activity heat, check-in volume, point density, unique users, or Top-K active geohash regions from trajectory records.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_region_heat/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to compute trajectory-based isochrones, reachable areas, travel-time accessibility, radiation range, or real mobility coverage from a starting geohash.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>anonymize_trajectory_data</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to anonymize, desensitize, privacy-protect, differentially perturb, k-anonymize, hash user IDs, grid-generalize, or prepare sensitive GPS/check-in trajectory data before retrieval or LLM analysis.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/anonymize_trajectory_data/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>classify_trajectory_state</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to classify each user's trajectory into motion states such as stationary, directed migration, frequent circulation, random walk, cruising, long-stay, or semantic mobility behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/classify_trajectory_state/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>clean_trajectory</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to clean raw GPS, check-in, signaling, taxi, or user mobility trajectory files by validating coordinates and timestamps, removing duplicates, filtering abnormal speed jumps, and exporting standardized cleaned trajectory points.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/clean_trajectory/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_flow_anomaly</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to detect macro-level mobility flow anomalies, including abnormal region heat, check-in spikes, OD flow spikes, sudden decreases, or unusual time-window activity.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_flow_anomaly/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_route_anomaly</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to detect individual trip or route anomalies, such as unusually long distance, unusually long/short duration, abnormal average speed, detours, or trips that deviate from a user's usual behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_route_anomaly/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_trajectory_cooccurrence</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to detect co-occurrence, companion trajectories, contact tracing, crowd gathering, group convergence, or multiple users appearing in the same space-time window.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_trajectory_cooccurrence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>extract_stay_points</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to extract stay points, dwell events, OD endpoints, or meaningful stops from GPS, check-in, signaling, taxi, or cleaned trajectory data.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/extract_stay_points/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>forecast_region_flow</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to predict future people or vehicle flow for target regions, based on historical regional activity series or raw trajectory points.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/forecast_region_flow/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>fuse_spatial_evidence</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to combine hotspot, anomaly, profile, forecast, and event-impact outputs into a unified ranked regional evidence view.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/fuse_spatial_evidence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>map_spatial_grid</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to map latitude/longitude trajectory records, staypoints, trips, or check-ins into spatial grids such as Geohash for aggregation and downstream spatial analysis.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/map_spatial_grid/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>measure_spatiotemporal_entropy</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to measure spatiotemporal entropy, mobility diversity, regional vitality, flow complexity, inflow-outflow variety, or urban activity index.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/measure_spatiotemporal_entropy/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>mine_trajectory_patterns</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to discover frequent travel patterns, recurring commuting sequences, repeated geohash chains, or multi-stop trip patterns from staypoints.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/mine_trajectory_patterns/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>predict_next_location</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to predict next location, next stop, future geohash, likely destination, destination inference, or Markov-chain mobility prediction from historical trajectories.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/predict_next_location/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>profile_urban_region</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to identify urban functional regions such as residential, commercial, transit, leisure, or mixed-use areas by combining trajectory activity and POI evidence.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/profile_urban_region/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>search_similar_trajectory</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to find historical trips or trajectory records similar to a target trip based on start/end position, travel distance, and duration.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/search_similar_trajectory/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>search_spatiotemporal</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to search or recall trajectory records by time window, hour range, geohash prefix, bounding box, city, or semantic text condition.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/search_spatiotemporal/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"3788c1f8-3735-4ef7-8a93-6766710aa782"}],"viewed_images":{},"intent_context":{"intent":"task","original_query":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。","normalized_query":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。","routing_query":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。","scene":"spatiotemporal_trajectory","scene_name":"时空轨迹","params":{},"scene_mode":"multi","scenes":["spatiotemporal_trajectory","video_surveillance"],"task_spans":[{"task_span_id":"span_a093da","text":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。"}],"planning_steps":[{"task_span_id":"span_b9b4ca","text":"读取输入视频文件，解析帧率、分辨率与时间戳基准，按固定采样间隔提取关键帧并建立帧序列索引，产出可供视觉模型逐帧处理的结构化帧数据集"},{"task_span_id":"span_fefc10","text":"调用视频监控场景的目标检测能力，在每一帧中定位潜在目标区域并按预设类别阈值进行筛选，输出仅包含“人员”与“车辆”两类对象的边界框坐标及置信度指标"},{"task_span_id":"span_294248","text":"依托时空轨迹分析能力，将连续帧中的同类别检测框进行跨帧关联与身份ID维护，依据坐标偏移量计算运动方向与步长特征，生成带唯一标识的时序位置记录序列"},{"task_span_id":"span_19f0b6","text":"对关联后的轨迹数据进行完整性校验与噪声过滤，剔除坐标突变或断链片段，按照对象类别、精确时间戳及路径点阵格式进行标准化重组，形成可回溯的结构化轨迹表"},{"task_span_id":"span_9284d6","text":"汇总全量目标的类别标签、时间序列与完整运动轨迹数据，按统一Schema导出为数据文件或API响应格式，确保字段映射清晰并满足下游系统调用要求"}],"scene_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_595dd8","scene":"spatiotemporal_trajectory","scene_name":"时空轨迹","text":"持续记录人员及车辆的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据","params":{}},{"sub_task_id":"sub_41c066","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","text":"识别视频里的人员和车辆","params":{}}],"sub_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_595dd8","scene":"spatiotemporal_trajectory","scene_name":"时空轨迹","text":"持续记录人员及车辆的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据","params":{}},{"sub_task_id":"sub_41c066","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","text":"识别视频里的人员和车辆","params":{}}],"task_hints":[],"mentioned_skill_ids":[],"confidence":0.9,"reason":"llm_scene_slot_rewrite","_source_message_key":"id:18ed18cd-409d-4ef7-a5db-3b2f8147e62a"},"routing_context":{"route_mode":"scene_filter","trigger":true,"primary_goal":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。","scene_tasks":[{"scene_task_id":"task_001","segment_id":"seg_001","segment_text":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。","scene":"spatiotemporal_trajectory","input_refs":[],"task_types":[],"selected_skills":[{"id":"analyze_event_impact","role":"primary","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"analyze_od_flow","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"analyze_region_heat","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"anonymize_trajectory_data","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"classify_trajectory_state","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"clean_trajectory","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"detect_flow_anomaly","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"detect_route_anomaly","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"detect_trajectory_cooccurrence","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"extract_stay_points","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"forecast_region_flow","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"fuse_spatial_evidence","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"map_spatial_grid","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"measure_spatiotemporal_entropy","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"mine_trajectory_patterns","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"predict_next_location","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"profile_urban_region","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"search_similar_trajectory","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"search_spatiotemporal","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null}],"expected_outputs":[],"depends_on":[]}],"global_selected_skills":["analyze_event_impact","analyze_od_flow","analyze_region_heat","analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility","anonymize_trajectory_data","classify_trajectory_state","clean_trajectory","detect_flow_anomaly","detect_route_anomaly","detect_trajectory_cooccurrence","extract_stay_points","forecast_region_flow","fuse_spatial_evidence","map_spatial_grid","measure_spatiotemporal_entropy","mine_trajectory_patterns","predict_next_location","profile_urban_region","search_similar_trajectory","search_spatiotemporal"],"default_public_skill_ids":[],"global_allowed_tools":[],"confidence":1.0,"route_reason":"SkillRouter disabled; injected all custom skills for detected intent scene as LeadAgent candidate skills","allowed_skills":["analyze_event_impact","analyze_od_flow","analyze_region_heat","analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility","anonymize_trajectory_data","classify_trajectory_state","clean_trajectory","detect_flow_anomaly","detect_route_anomaly","detect_trajectory_cooccurrence","extract_stay_points","forecast_region_flow","fuse_spatial_evidence","map_spatial_grid","measure_spatiotemporal_entropy","mine_trajectory_patterns","predict_next_location","profile_urban_region","search_similar_trajectory","search_spatiotemporal"],"selection_owner":"lead_agent","_source_message_key":"id:18ed18cd-409d-4ef7-a5db-3b2f8147e62a"},"dialogue_context":{"act":"new_task","confidence":0.7,"reason":"no_pending_action_match","parsed_answer":null,"pending_action_id":null,"resume_intent_context":null,"resume_routing_context":null,"metadata":{}},"final_scope_skill_ids":["analyze_event_impact","analyze_od_flow","analyze_region_heat","analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility","anonymize_trajectory_data","classify_trajectory_state","clean_trajectory","detect_flow_anomaly","detect_route_anomaly","detect_trajectory_cooccurrence","extract_stay_points","forecast_region_flow","fuse_spatial_evidence","map_spatial_grid","measure_spatiotemporal_entropy","mine_trajectory_patterns","predict_next_location","profile_urban_region","search_similar_trajectory","search_spatiotemporal"],"allowed_tool_names":[]}

event: values
data: {"messages":[{"content":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"18ed18cd-409d-4ef7-a5db-3b2f8147e62a"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_event_impact</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to evaluate the impact of an external event such as rainstorm, sports event, traffic control, holiday, emergency, or policy intervention on regional trajectory volume.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_event_impact/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_od_flow</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks for OD flow analysis, origin-destination matrices, commute corridors, migration routes, or region-to-region movement aggregation from staypoints.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_od_flow/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_region_heat</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to compute regional activity heat, check-in volume, point density, unique users, or Top-K active geohash regions from trajectory records.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_region_heat/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to compute trajectory-based isochrones, reachable areas, travel-time accessibility, radiation range, or real mobility coverage from a starting geohash.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>anonymize_trajectory_data</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to anonymize, desensitize, privacy-protect, differentially perturb, k-anonymize, hash user IDs, grid-generalize, or prepare sensitive GPS/check-in trajectory data before retrieval or LLM analysis.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/anonymize_trajectory_data/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>classify_trajectory_state</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to classify each user's trajectory into motion states such as stationary, directed migration, frequent circulation, random walk, cruising, long-stay, or semantic mobility behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/classify_trajectory_state/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>clean_trajectory</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to clean raw GPS, check-in, signaling, taxi, or user mobility trajectory files by validating coordinates and timestamps, removing duplicates, filtering abnormal speed jumps, and exporting standardized cleaned trajectory points.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/clean_trajectory/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_flow_anomaly</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to detect macro-level mobility flow anomalies, including abnormal region heat, check-in spikes, OD flow spikes, sudden decreases, or unusual time-window activity.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_flow_anomaly/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_route_anomaly</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to detect individual trip or route anomalies, such as unusually long distance, unusually long/short duration, abnormal average speed, detours, or trips that deviate from a user's usual behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_route_anomaly/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_trajectory_cooccurrence</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to detect co-occurrence, companion trajectories, contact tracing, crowd gathering, group convergence, or multiple users appearing in the same space-time window.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_trajectory_cooccurrence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>extract_stay_points</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to extract stay points, dwell events, OD endpoints, or meaningful stops from GPS, check-in, signaling, taxi, or cleaned trajectory data.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/extract_stay_points/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>forecast_region_flow</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to predict future people or vehicle flow for target regions, based on historical regional activity series or raw trajectory points.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/forecast_region_flow/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>fuse_spatial_evidence</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to combine hotspot, anomaly, profile, forecast, and event-impact outputs into a unified ranked regional evidence view.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/fuse_spatial_evidence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>map_spatial_grid</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to map latitude/longitude trajectory records, staypoints, trips, or check-ins into spatial grids such as Geohash for aggregation and downstream spatial analysis.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/map_spatial_grid/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>measure_spatiotemporal_entropy</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to measure spatiotemporal entropy, mobility diversity, regional vitality, flow complexity, inflow-outflow variety, or urban activity index.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/measure_spatiotemporal_entropy/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>mine_trajectory_patterns</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to discover frequent travel patterns, recurring commuting sequences, repeated geohash chains, or multi-stop trip patterns from staypoints.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/mine_trajectory_patterns/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>predict_next_location</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to predict next location, next stop, future geohash, likely destination, destination inference, or Markov-chain mobility prediction from historical trajectories.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/predict_next_location/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>profile_urban_region</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to identify urban functional regions such as residential, commercial, transit, leisure, or mixed-use areas by combining trajectory activity and POI evidence.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/profile_urban_region/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>search_similar_trajectory</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to find historical trips or trajectory records similar to a target trip based on start/end position, travel distance, and duration.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/search_similar_trajectory/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>search_spatiotemporal</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to search or recall trajectory records by time window, hour range, geohash prefix, bounding box, city, or semantic text condition.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/search_spatiotemporal/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"3788c1f8-3735-4ef7-8a93-6766710aa782"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。\n识别场景：时空轨迹 (spatiotemporal_trajectory)；场景模式：multi；候选场景：spatiotemporal_trajectory, video_surveillance\n任务切分：\n- 请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。\n任务规划：\n1. 读取输入视频文件，解析帧率、分辨率与时间戳基准，按固定采样间隔提取关键帧并建立帧序列索引，产出可供视觉模型逐帧处理的结构化帧数据集\n2. 调用视频监控场景的目标检测能力，在每一帧中定位潜在目标区域并按预设类别阈值进行筛选，输出仅包含“人员”与“车辆”两类对象的边界框坐标及置信度指标\n3. 依托时空轨迹分析能力，将连续帧中的同类别检测框进行跨帧关联与身份ID维护，依据坐标偏移量计算运动方向与步长特征，生成带唯一标识的时序位置记录序列\n4. 对关联后的轨迹数据进行完整性校验与噪声过滤，剔除坐标突变或断链片段，按照对象类别、精确时间戳及路径点阵格式进行标准化重组，形成可回溯的结构化轨迹表\n5. 汇总全量目标的类别标签、时间序列与完整运动轨迹数据，按统一Schema导出为数据文件或API响应格式，确保字段映射清晰并满足下游系统调用要求\n场景任务：\n- spatiotemporal_trajectory: 持续记录人员及车辆的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据\n- video_surveillance: 识别视频里的人员和车辆\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"3e14e93e-31ce-4511-94e9-c119a9ab6bcd"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":361,"prompt_tokens":12494,"total_tokens":12855,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":202,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":361},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":12494}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-cf2b82d6-9b3f-99b8-8ea7-e3f4f26aae22","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f8f6c-2c35-7841-975d-30cf4d3853a8-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"ask_clarification","args":{"question":"请提供需要分析的视频文件路径或名称。您是希望我：(1) 在本地数据目录中查找视频文件，还是 (2) 您有特定的视频文件需要上传？另外，是否需要重点关注特定类型的目标（如仅行人、仅车辆，或全部类型）？","clarification_type":"missing_info","context":"需要视频文件才能执行目标检测和轨迹跟踪分析","options":"[\"在 /mnt/datasets 中查找视频文件\", \"我将上传视频文件\", \"其他路径\"]"},"id":"call_a1ca61d59bf84464b905d397","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":12494,"output_tokens":361,"total_tokens":12855,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":202}}}],"thread_data":{"workspace_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/30f29ae5-9eae-480a-b1ac-6a9ecb1fae58/user-data/workspace","uploads_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/30f29ae5-9eae-480a-b1ac-6a9ecb1fae58/user-data/uploads","outputs_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/30f29ae5-9eae-480a-b1ac-6a9ecb1fae58/user-data/outputs"},"artifacts":[],"raw_messages":[{"content":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"18ed18cd-409d-4ef7-a5db-3b2f8147e62a"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_event_impact</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to evaluate the impact of an external event such as rainstorm, sports event, traffic control, holiday, emergency, or policy intervention on regional trajectory volume.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_event_impact/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_od_flow</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks for OD flow analysis, origin-destination matrices, commute corridors, migration routes, or region-to-region movement aggregation from staypoints.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_od_flow/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_region_heat</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to compute regional activity heat, check-in volume, point density, unique users, or Top-K active geohash regions from trajectory records.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_region_heat/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to compute trajectory-based isochrones, reachable areas, travel-time accessibility, radiation range, or real mobility coverage from a starting geohash.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>anonymize_trajectory_data</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to anonymize, desensitize, privacy-protect, differentially perturb, k-anonymize, hash user IDs, grid-generalize, or prepare sensitive GPS/check-in trajectory data before retrieval or LLM analysis.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/anonymize_trajectory_data/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>classify_trajectory_state</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to classify each user's trajectory into motion states such as stationary, directed migration, frequent circulation, random walk, cruising, long-stay, or semantic mobility behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/classify_trajectory_state/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>clean_trajectory</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to clean raw GPS, check-in, signaling, taxi, or user mobility trajectory files by validating coordinates and timestamps, removing duplicates, filtering abnormal speed jumps, and exporting standardized cleaned trajectory points.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/clean_trajectory/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_flow_anomaly</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to detect macro-level mobility flow anomalies, including abnormal region heat, check-in spikes, OD flow spikes, sudden decreases, or unusual time-window activity.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_flow_anomaly/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_route_anomaly</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to detect individual trip or route anomalies, such as unusually long distance, unusually long/short duration, abnormal average speed, detours, or trips that deviate from a user's usual behavior.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_route_anomaly/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>detect_trajectory_cooccurrence</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to detect co-occurrence, companion trajectories, contact tracing, crowd gathering, group convergence, or multiple users appearing in the same space-time window.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/detect_trajectory_cooccurrence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>extract_stay_points</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to extract stay points, dwell events, OD endpoints, or meaningful stops from GPS, check-in, signaling, taxi, or cleaned trajectory data.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/extract_stay_points/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>forecast_region_flow</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to predict future people or vehicle flow for target regions, based on historical regional activity series or raw trajectory points.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/forecast_region_flow/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>fuse_spatial_evidence</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to combine hotspot, anomaly, profile, forecast, and event-impact outputs into a unified ranked regional evidence view.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/fuse_spatial_evidence/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>map_spatial_grid</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to map latitude/longitude trajectory records, staypoints, trips, or check-ins into spatial grids such as Geohash for aggregation and downstream spatial analysis.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/map_spatial_grid/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>measure_spatiotemporal_entropy</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to measure spatiotemporal entropy, mobility diversity, regional vitality, flow complexity, inflow-outflow variety, or urban activity index.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/measure_spatiotemporal_entropy/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>mine_trajectory_patterns</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to discover frequent travel patterns, recurring commuting sequences, repeated geohash chains, or multi-stop trip patterns from staypoints.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/mine_trajectory_patterns/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>predict_next_location</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user asks to predict next location, next stop, future geohash, likely destination, destination inference, or Markov-chain mobility prediction from historical trajectories.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/predict_next_location/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>profile_urban_region</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to identify urban functional regions such as residential, commercial, transit, leisure, or mixed-use areas by combining trajectory activity and POI evidence.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/profile_urban_region/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>search_similar_trajectory</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to find historical trips or trajectory records similar to a target trip based on start/end position, travel distance, and duration.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/search_similar_trajectory/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>search_spatiotemporal</name>\n      <description>Use this skill when the user wants to search or recall trajectory records by time window, hour range, geohash prefix, bounding box, city, or semantic text condition.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/spatiotemporal_trajectory/search_spatiotemporal/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"3788c1f8-3735-4ef7-8a93-6766710aa782"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。\n识别场景：时空轨迹 (spatiotemporal_trajectory)；场景模式：multi；候选场景：spatiotemporal_trajectory, video_surveillance\n任务切分：\n- 请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。\n任务规划：\n1. 读取输入视频文件，解析帧率、分辨率与时间戳基准，按固定采样间隔提取关键帧并建立帧序列索引，产出可供视觉模型逐帧处理的结构化帧数据集\n2. 调用视频监控场景的目标检测能力，在每一帧中定位潜在目标区域并按预设类别阈值进行筛选，输出仅包含“人员”与“车辆”两类对象的边界框坐标及置信度指标\n3. 依托时空轨迹分析能力，将连续帧中的同类别检测框进行跨帧关联与身份ID维护，依据坐标偏移量计算运动方向与步长特征，生成带唯一标识的时序位置记录序列\n4. 对关联后的轨迹数据进行完整性校验与噪声过滤，剔除坐标突变或断链片段，按照对象类别、精确时间戳及路径点阵格式进行标准化重组，形成可回溯的结构化轨迹表\n5. 汇总全量目标的类别标签、时间序列与完整运动轨迹数据，按统一Schema导出为数据文件或API响应格式，确保字段映射清晰并满足下游系统调用要求\n场景任务：\n- spatiotemporal_trajectory: 持续记录人员及车辆的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据\n- video_surveillance: 识别视频里的人员和车辆\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"3e14e93e-31ce-4511-94e9-c119a9ab6bcd"},{"content":"","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":361,"prompt_tokens":12494,"total_tokens":12855,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":202,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":361},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":12494}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-cf2b82d6-9b3f-99b8-8ea7-e3f4f26aae22","finish_reason":"tool_calls","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f8f6c-2c35-7841-975d-30cf4d3853a8-0","tool_calls":[{"name":"ask_clarification","args":{"question":"请提供需要分析的视频文件路径或名称。您是希望我：(1) 在本地数据目录中查找视频文件，还是 (2) 您有特定的视频文件需要上传？另外，是否需要重点关注特定类型的目标（如仅行人、仅车辆，或全部类型）？","clarification_type":"missing_info","context":"需要视频文件才能执行目标检测和轨迹跟踪分析","options":"[\"在 /mnt/datasets 中查找视频文件\", \"我将上传视频文件\", \"其他路径\"]"},"id":"call_a1ca61d59bf84464b905d397","type":"tool_call"}],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":12494,"output_tokens":361,"total_tokens":12855,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":202}}}],"viewed_images":{},"intent_context":{"intent":"task","original_query":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。","normalized_query":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。","routing_query":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。","scene":"spatiotemporal_trajectory","scene_name":"时空轨迹","params":{},"scene_mode":"multi","scenes":["spatiotemporal_trajectory","video_surveillance"],"task_spans":[{"task_span_id":"span_a093da","text":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。"}],"planning_steps":[{"task_span_id":"span_b9b4ca","text":"读取输入视频文件，解析帧率、分辨率与时间戳基准，按固定采样间隔提取关键帧并建立帧序列索引，产出可供视觉模型逐帧处理的结构化帧数据集"},{"task_span_id":"span_fefc10","text":"调用视频监控场景的目标检测能力，在每一帧中定位潜在目标区域并按预设类别阈值进行筛选，输出仅包含“人员”与“车辆”两类对象的边界框坐标及置信度指标"},{"task_span_id":"span_294248","text":"依托时空轨迹分析能力，将连续帧中的同类别检测框进行跨帧关联与身份ID维护，依据坐标偏移量计算运动方向与步长特征，生成带唯一标识的时序位置记录序列"},{"task_span_id":"span_19f0b6","text":"对关联后的轨迹数据进行完整性校验与噪声过滤，剔除坐标突变或断链片段，按照对象类别、精确时间戳及路径点阵格式进行标准化重组，形成可回溯的结构化轨迹表"},{"task_span_id":"span_9284d6","text":"汇总全量目标的类别标签、时间序列与完整运动轨迹数据，按统一Schema导出为数据文件或API响应格式，确保字段映射清晰并满足下游系统调用要求"}],"scene_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_595dd8","scene":"spatiotemporal_trajectory","scene_name":"时空轨迹","text":"持续记录人员及车辆的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据","params":{}},{"sub_task_id":"sub_41c066","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","text":"识别视频里的人员和车辆","params":{}}],"sub_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_595dd8","scene":"spatiotemporal_trajectory","scene_name":"时空轨迹","text":"持续记录人员及车辆的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据","params":{}},{"sub_task_id":"sub_41c066","scene":"video_surveillance","scene_name":"视频监控","text":"识别视频里的人员和车辆","params":{}}],"task_hints":[],"mentioned_skill_ids":[],"confidence":0.9,"reason":"llm_scene_slot_rewrite","_source_message_key":"id:18ed18cd-409d-4ef7-a5db-3b2f8147e62a"},"routing_context":{"route_mode":"scene_filter","trigger":true,"primary_goal":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。","scene_tasks":[{"scene_task_id":"task_001","segment_id":"seg_001","segment_text":"请识别视频里的人员和车辆，持续记录它们的位置和运动轨迹，并输出对象类别、时间和轨迹数据。","scene":"spatiotemporal_trajectory","input_refs":[],"task_types":[],"selected_skills":[{"id":"analyze_event_impact","role":"primary","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"analyze_od_flow","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"analyze_region_heat","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"analyze_spatiotemporal_accessibility","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"anonymize_trajectory_data","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"classify_trajectory_state","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"clean_trajectory","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"detect_flow_anomaly","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"detect_route_anomaly","role":"supporting","s